1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,310
In Gravedawn, the fog comes early.

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:05,937
Salt rings every doorstep.

3
00:00:05,937 --> 00:00:08,668
Empty windows watch the street.

4
00:00:08,668 --> 00:00:13,138
And on the hill, the tower waits — patient as an executioner.

5
00:00:13,138 --> 00:00:16,209
People vanish between dusk and dawn.

6
00:00:16,209 --> 00:00:18,274
Doors found open.

7
00:00:18,274 --> 00:00:20,529
Lamps still burning.

8
00:00:20,529 --> 00:00:23,152
No bodies left behind.

9
00:00:23,152 --> 00:00:25,855
Priests bless the thresholds.

10
00:00:25,855 --> 00:00:28,627
Families pack what they can carry.

11
00:00:28,627 --> 00:00:34,144
The rest stay, redraw their wards each morning, and try not to look at the hill.

12
00:00:34,144 --> 00:00:37,350
Winter’s longest night is nearly here.

13
00:00:37,350 --> 00:00:48,070
Five adventurers ride toward a town that has stopped believing in hope — and toward a curse that has outlived every sword, every prayer, every brave fool who climbed to meet it.

14
00:00:48,070 --> 00:00:55,461
When the bell tolls at midnight… will they cleanse what waits in the stone — or become another name scratched from the ledger?

15
00:00:55,461 --> 00:00:58,002
The Bell Tolls at Midnight.

16
00:00:58,002 --> 00:01:00,448
A dark fantasy story.

17
00:01:00,448 --> 00:01:04,415
Coming soon — read it when the tale is fully told.

